course: dictionary
lesson: 6400
title: Murky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Murky» means dark and dirty, so you cannot see through it. Look at the words around it for clues: «In the murky water an elephantnose fish cannot see.» If the fish cannot see, the water must be dark and hard to see through.
explain: «Murky» can also describe air or light that is dark and foggy. It can even describe something that is not clear, like «the rules are murky». Try your meaning in the sentence: "the rules are dark and hard to see through" does not quite fit, but "the rules are unclear and hard to understand" does, so that is the meaning here.
explain: Animals have clever ways to deal with murky water. «A dolphin in murky water clicks, and the echoes come back through its lower jaw to its ears.» The dolphin does not need to see, because it finds things by sound.
fact: «Murky» is an adjective. Its forms are murky, murkier and murkiest.
fact: «Murky» means dark and dirty, so you cannot see through it, as in «murky water».
fact: «Murky» can also mean not clear, or secret and suspicious, as in «a murky past».
fact: Good phrases to remember are murky water, murky depths and murky details.
fact: Electric eels send out weak electric pulses to sense things in murky water, and bats and dolphins use echoes to find things in the dark.
exercise: «In the murky water an elephantnose fish cannot see.» What does murky mean here? | *Dark and dirty, so you cannot see through it | Bright and sparkling clear | Hot and steaming | Frozen solid
exercise: «Swimmers are told to avoid murky river mouths.» Why is murky water dangerous for swimmers? | Fish always bite in warm water | *You cannot see how deep it is | It is too salty to swim in
exercise: The news report said the details were murky. What does murky mean here? | Loud and cheerful | *Unclear and hard to understand | Bright and shiny | Sweet and sticky
test: «The fog made the streets look murky at dawn.» What does murky mean? | Very loud | Sweet-smelling | Full of bright colours | *Dark and gloomy
test: What do bats and dolphins use to find things in murky water? | Smell | *Echoes that bounce back | Touch with their tails | Sight from bright lights
exam: «A murky past» means what? | *A dark, secret past that people doubt | A past full of sunshine and holidays | A past that is easy to see clearly | A cheerful, happy past
